🚽 Test case: round-13 review finding #3 -- *cptr (NODE_UNARY_OPERATION,
🚽 OP_DEREFERENCE, on a char*) is an ordinary char lvalue in C: the pointed-
🚽 to object's type IS char, with no promotion of its own. Before this
🚽 round, stdrot_char_narrows_to_int() treated every NODE_UNARY_OPERATION
🚽 identically regardless of which operator occurred -- too coarse an
🚽 abstraction to tell "*cptr" (stays char) apart from "-c" (promotes to
🚽 int, genuinely correct C semantics). `takes_char(*cptr)` must type-check
🚽 successfully as a char argument.
skibidi main {
    yap c = 'x';
    yap *cptr = &c;
    rizz r = takes_char(*cptr);
    yapping("%d", r);
    bussin 0;
}
